(D5 — Discrepancy 5 repro: a DECLARED `float` or `map` return type is lost
 when the call result is printed directly rather than routed through a
 declared variable. The float prints as its IEEE-754 bit pattern
 (4612811918334230528 = 0x4004000000000000 = 2.5) and the map as a raw
 heap address; the same two values print correctly one line earlier, out
 of variables of the declared type. text, boolean and list are unaffected
 (FUN-40). This is the shape of vox bug #45, except that #45 says
 declaring the return type is the cure — here it is declared and the
 result is still wrong. The map address varies per run, so this probe is
 compared on its EXIT CODE: it exits 3 unconditionally after printing.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D5.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   2.5
   {"ann": 30}
   --- the same two calls, printed directly ---
   4612811918334230528
   140201717768192
   exit 3
)
To 'give float'. Return a float, 2.5.
To 'give map'. Return a map, {"ann": 30}.

a float called 'routed float' is 'give float'.
a map called 'routed map' is 'give map'.
Print 'routed float'.
Print 'routed map'.
Print "--- the same two calls, printed directly ---".
Print 'give float'.
Print 'give map'.
Exit 3.
